1. What is the difference between precision and recall?
Precision:
=>Out of all predicted positive (diabetic) cases, how many are actually positive?
 Precision = TP / TP + FP
=>Focus: Prediction correctness
=>High precision → fewer false positives

Recall:
=>Out of all actual positive (diabetic) cases, how many did we correctly detect?
 Recall = TP / TP + FN
=>Focus: Capturing all real positives
=>High recall → fewer false negatives

2. What is cross-validation, and why is it important in binary classification?
Cross-validation is a technique used to evaluate a model by splitting the dataset into multiple parts (folds) and training/testing the model multiple times.
Most common type: K-Fold Cross-Validation
=>Data is divided into K equal parts (folds)
=>Model is trained on K-1 folds
=>Tested on the remaining fold
=>This process repeats K times
=>Final performance = average of all runs

Why is it Important in Binary Classification?
 1. Better Performance Estimate
 2. Reduces Overfitting
 3. Uses Data Efficiently
 4. Helps Model Selection
 5. Handles Class Imbalance Better